From c959e7a4a2068376b48c1cc8de1697b6a7f2f17a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 05:08:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 30/85] render: hierarchy the way Wallpaper Engine does

Decoded from wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485: the "effectively visible" test
(GH 0x1401b50e0), the image model matrix (GH 0x1402277d0) and the
alignment offset (GH 0x140230a80).

Visibility. An object is drawn only when it and every ancestor are
visible: WE's test is its own visible bit AND, recursively, the parent's,
and the image, text and particle render paths (and the particle step's
reset, GH 0x140255d00) all ask it. LWE read only the object's own
`visible`, so the children of a hidden group or image drew (12 of the
owner's scenes have a visible child under a hidden ancestor).
CScene::isEffectivelyVisible is the one test, also used for the active
camera object. Also: an image's last pass went to the screen only if the
image was visible while its passes were built, so an image hidden at load,
by itself or a parent, never showed when a property or script turned it
on. The pass is now always built for the screen; render () skips a hidden
image every frame.

Particle parents. A particle system's origin, scale and z angle are in
its parent's space, like an image's (every object shares WE's one base
transform with a parent, GH 0x14020dcc0): CImage's parent walk moved to
CObject (resolveTransform, localTransform, which now reads a particle's
own scale and angles), and CParticle resolves its place every frame, so it
follows a moving, animated or scripted parent (or origin). Its own x/y
angles stay its own. World-space control points stay put in the world.
Before, the origin was the raw local one, read once at setup.

Rotation pivot. An aligned image turns (and scales) about its origin, its
anchor point: WE's model matrix is the object's transform times a
translation by the alignment offset (+-size/2 per side). LWE turned it
about the centre of the shifted quad. Centred images are unchanged.

Not done: text objects still ignore their parent's transform (CText,
redrawn in B4); a sound object under a hidden parent keeps playing (whether
WE silences it was not settled).

Origin: ours
Why: children of hidden groups drew, particle systems ignored their parent and stayed where they were set up, and aligned layers turned about the wrong point (docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B6: G03, G04 particles, P36, G31)
